# ANCHOR RUNTIME-ARTIFACT DIRECTORY RULES WITH A LEADING SLASH.
#
# `logs/` (no leading slash) matches a directory called `logs` at ANY depth, so
# it silently swallowed the SOURCE package `src/services/execution/logs/`.
# Three files there — including its `__init__.py` — were never committed: git
# status shows nothing, because that is exactly what ignoring means. A fresh
# clone lost the package and 144 tests failed on an import error that read like
# test rot. `/logs/` matches only src/backend/logs/, which is what was meant.
#
# The same mistake is already recorded below for `lib/`. If you add a rule for a
# generated directory, anchor it.

# Logs
/logs/
*.log

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.so
.Python
env/
build/
develop-eggs/
dist/
downloads/
eggs/
.eggs/
# Anchored, for the reason at the top of this file. Unanchored, `lib/` matched
# the export template's REAL frontend source dirs (shadcn utils, markdown
# renderer, deck themes) and had to be undone with four negation lines — which
# then rotted silently when the refactor moved the template out of
# src/engines/, leaving a new file there swallowable all over again. A venv's
# lib/ is at the root; anchoring says so and needs no exceptions.
/lib/
/lib64/
parts/
sdist/
var/
*.egg-info/
.installed.cfg
*.egg

# Virtual Environment
venv/
.env
.venv
ENV/

# IDE
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo

# Database
*.sqlite3
*.db

# Alembic
alembic/versions/

# Local development
.DS_Store
.coverage
htmlcov/
.pytest_cache/

# CrewAI unified cognitive memory stores (per-crew local LanceDB) — never commit
# user data. Matches the CREWAI_STORAGE_DIR naming that
# CrewMemoryService.setup_storage_directory emits.
kasal_default_*/
kasal_databricks_*/
kasal_lakebase_*/
**/memories.lance/
**/memories.lance/**

# import-linter graph cache
.import_linter_cache/

# Everything a test run writes — logs, memory, scratch DBs.
# The pollution guard in tests/conftest.py asserts nothing lands outside this.
tests/.artifacts/
